# LLC30 adjoint experiment: based on V4r6's own real data.smooth values
# (Time-invariant-adjoint/v4r6/input.V4r6.102/data.smooth), with ONE real
# correction found only by actually running the model: V4r6's own
# smooth2Dsize(1)=2 / smooth3DsizeH(1)=3 / smooth3DsizeZ(1)=3 are NOT
# parameter-only as an earlier draft of this file claimed -- confirmed in
# pkg/smooth/smooth_init2d.F/smooth_init3d.F, those exact values (2 for
# 2D, 3 for 3D) gate reading POSITION-VARYING smoothing-scale files from
# disk (smooth2Dscales001, smooth3DscalesH001, smooth3DscalesZ001),
# which are real V4r6 production files at LLC90 resolution this project
# never coarsened to LLC30 (confirmed via a real STOP ABNORMAL END:
# MDS_READ_FIELD smooth2Dscales001.data when first run with the
# verbatim-copied value). Fixed by using size=0 (CONSTANT scale,
# smooth2D_Lx0/Ly0 and smooth3D_Lx0/Ly0/Lz0 below) instead -- these are
# runtime &SMOOTH_NML values, not CPP flags, so no rebuild is needed.
# The constant values used are the real V4r6 production scale files'
# own domain-mean magnitudes (confirmed by direct inspection of
# smooth2Dscales001/smooth3DscalesH001/smooth3DscalesZ001: horizontal
# Lx/Ly mean ~191,400 m, vertical Lz mean ~236 m) -- a documented
# simplification (flat representative scale instead of the real
# position-varying field), same pattern as Phase A's GM_background_K
# scalar substitution for GM_*3dFile.
 &SMOOTH_NML
 smooth2Dnbt(1)=300
 smooth2Dtype(1)=1
 smooth2Dsize(1)=0
 smooth2D_Lx0(1)=191400.,
 smooth2D_Ly0(1)=191400.,
 smooth2Dfilter(1)=0
 smooth3Dnbt(1)=300
 smooth3DtypeH(1)=1
 smooth3DsizeH(1)=0
 smooth3D_Lx0(1)=191400.,
 smooth3D_Ly0(1)=191400.,
 smooth3DtypeZ(1)=1
 smooth3DsizeZ(1)=0
 smooth3D_Lz0(1)=236.25,
 smooth3Dfilter(1)=0
 /
